WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.976
- We are back with Garth Brooks,

00:00:01.976 --> 00:00:05.157
give it up, everybody!
(audience cheers)

00:00:05.157 --> 00:00:07.710
Here about Garth working with
Dolly for the first time.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.928
He's done this at such a
high level for so long,

00:00:09.928 --> 00:00:12.937
we thought it'd be fun to
throw some random musical names

00:00:12.937 --> 00:00:15.420
at him to see what his memories

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.800
and stories are with those people.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.633
So here we go.

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:18.466
Good luck.

00:00:18.466 --> 00:00:21.360
In honor of his residency,
Garth Brooks Plus One

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.670
that starts tonight at Caesar's Palace,

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:24.990
we are adding a Vegas twist.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:25.860
You're welcome.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.563
This is Rockstar Roulette.

00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:30.392
(country music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:33.752
♪ Rockstar Roulette ♪

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:35.520
- I'll press this button
though and the roulette wheel

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.290
will spin, and whatever name pops up,

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.450
Garth has to tell a
story about that person.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.415
Don't fail us, let's go.

00:00:41.415 --> 00:00:43.140
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.160
- [Kelly] So here it is.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.390
- [Garth] Who is it?

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.619
- [Kelly] I don't know.

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:47.452
(bell dings)

00:00:47.452 --> 00:00:48.285
Ed Sheeran!

00:00:48.285 --> 00:00:49.500
Do you like Ed Sheeran?

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.611
- Oh great, I love Ed Sheeran.

00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:51.985
- (gasps) I love Ed Sheeran.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.818
- I love Ed Sheeran, because you know,

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:55.617
when you talk about Vegas,
Garth Brooks in Vegas, right?

00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:58.200
1400 seats, right?
- Yeah, it's great.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.033
- It's awesome.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:03.270
Ed Sheeran with just him
and a guitar, Croak Stadium,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.529
86,000 people.

00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:05.490
- [Kelly] I've seen him in an arena dome.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.450
- Oh my god.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.887
And it's just him in a guitar.

00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:11.680
And what I love with him,
what I love is Ed has,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.510
I don't even know how to explain this.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:18.360
You don't have to reinvent music.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.792
Okay, it's in the soul and it
just keeps getting recycled.

00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:24.120
(guitar strums)

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.680
It's simple, right?

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.513
- [Kelly] Oh, I know that song.

00:01:26.513 --> 00:01:28.354
- All the way back from, was it

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.854
♪ Oh my love ♪

00:01:33.585 --> 00:01:35.053
- I love this song

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:37.757
♪ My darling ♪

00:01:37.757 --> 00:01:38.590
Right.
- Yes.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.140
- Exactly, so it could come move,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.090
and it just keeps going
through the years, right.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.122
Like,

00:01:43.122 --> 00:01:46.415
♪ I heard about a secret chord ♪

00:01:46.415 --> 00:01:50.336
♪ That David played and
it pleased the Lord ♪

00:01:50.336 --> 00:01:55.336
♪ But you don't really
care for music do ya ♪

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.910
- Exactly.
- Jeff Buckey.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.447
- Right.
- I mean Leonard Cohen.

00:01:58.447 --> 00:01:59.551
- Come a little closer to

00:01:59.551 --> 00:02:01.917
♪ I got a girl crush ♪

00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:03.422
- Ah!

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:07.134
♪ I hate to admit it but ♪

00:02:07.134 --> 00:02:11.967
♪ I got a heart rush
just won't slow down ♪

00:02:14.144 --> 00:02:14.977
Right?
- Little Big Town, yeah.

00:02:14.977 --> 00:02:17.490
- Do it, let's come all the
way up now to this, right.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.153
Ed does it.

00:02:19.153 --> 00:02:21.090
♪ I found a love ♪

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.663
- I love Perfect, that's
what got your way in color.

00:02:23.663 --> 00:02:27.648
♪ For me ♪

00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:32.648
♪ Darling just dive right
in and follow me lead ♪

00:02:34.878 --> 00:02:37.012
♪ I met a girl ♪

00:02:37.012 --> 00:02:38.545
- Simple storytelling.

00:02:38.545 --> 00:02:41.937
♪ So beautiful and sweet ♪

00:02:41.937 --> 00:02:46.937
♪ I never knew you were the
someone waiting for me ♪

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.283
- If I'm gonna sing the high part,

00:02:49.283 --> 00:02:50.896
I'm gonna have to stand up,
so I'm gonna stop there.

00:02:50.896 --> 00:02:53.585
(Kelly laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:02:53.585 --> 00:02:54.959
- You're right, though.
- It is.

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:57.203
- It's those timeless classic
kinda melodies and chords.

00:02:57.203 --> 00:03:00.570
- Yeah, but it, that's
what I love about music.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:04.230
It's timeless and it's
timely at the same time.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.206
It just depends whose hands it's in.

00:03:06.206 --> 00:03:08.078
Those four particular hands

00:03:08.078 --> 00:03:09.990
when you talk about the songwriters.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.550
- Storytellers.
- Woo!

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.542
Fabulous.

00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:14.130
- I love that I said Buckley,
it was Leonard Cohen first,

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.015
the other song, but I was
like Hallelujah, yeah.

00:03:16.015 --> 00:03:18.300
I knew it, I think, 'cause
of Buckley, but yeah.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.233
Okay, we're gonna go next.

00:03:19.233 --> 00:03:21.519
That was gorgeous, of course.

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:23.010
- Oh we gotta do it again?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.551
- Yes, I'm gonna make
you keep, dance, monkey!

00:03:25.551 --> 00:03:27.101
(Garth laughs)

00:03:27.101 --> 00:03:28.478
Adele!
(audience cheers)

00:03:28.478 --> 00:03:30.059
Who doesn't love Adele?

00:03:30.059 --> 00:03:33.150
- Woo, this is tough.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:33.990
- I love her.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.480
- This is tough because the
story that comes to mind,

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.949
it's not a good one.

00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:39.030
- Wait, what?
(audience laughs)

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.960
- Yeah, I'm so sorry.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.410
My youngest, probably 12 years ago, 13,

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.817
my youngest came in from
school and she goes,

00:03:45.817 --> 00:03:49.447
"Dad, dad, you've got to
hear this song from Adele.

00:03:49.447 --> 00:03:51.100
"I've never heard a song like it."

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.050
I said, "Really?"

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:55.230
I said, what's it's name, says
"To Make You Feel My Love."

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.935
(audience laughs)

00:03:57.935 --> 00:03:59.310
I said, "You have to
be kidding me, right?"

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.143
No, I didn't, I didn't say anything.

00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:01.237
I said, "Oh really?

00:04:01.237 --> 00:04:02.414
"Tell me about it."

00:04:02.414 --> 00:04:03.390
(audience laughs)

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.982
People always ask, you know, well,

00:04:05.982 --> 00:04:07.215
which is her favorite version?

00:04:07.215 --> 00:04:10.095
I said, "I don't know, we
haven't spoke since that day."

00:04:10.095 --> 00:04:12.300
(audience laughs)

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.447
But oh my God, when she, because you

00:04:14.447 --> 00:04:18.870
♪ When the rain's blowing in your face ♪

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.212
- See, this is what I grew up on, yeah.

00:04:21.212 --> 00:04:26.212
♪ And the whole world is on your case ♪

00:04:26.717 --> 00:04:31.717
♪ I would offer you a warm embrace ♪

00:04:32.094 --> 00:04:35.677
♪ To make you feel my love ♪

00:04:37.295 --> 00:04:39.821
(audience cheers)
- Aw, I love that song.

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:40.800
- It's nice.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.079
And I gotta tell you,

00:04:42.079 --> 00:04:45.030
it's like anything that you cover right?

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.650
So it's like you, you're walking around,

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.333
going, Make You Feel My Love,

00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:50.091
I feel pretty good about my version.

00:04:50.091 --> 00:04:51.805
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:55.140
And then you hear Adele
singing, all of a sudden,

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.880
you're like, oh okay, I get it.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.540
That she just, everything
she touches just sings,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.373
it's beautiful.

00:05:01.373 --> 00:05:03.180
- But also it's, yes, absolutely.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.108
But also it's this sign
of such a great song.

00:05:06.108 --> 00:05:08.460
So many people have covered this song,

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.870
whether they've recorded it for a version

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.643
or just done it for a show.

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:14.190
Like that's a great song.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.410
And it's like, and it
depends on who's singing it.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.730
Like I grew up with your version

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.950
and it's like one of
those things that just,

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.805
it hits me like in such a different way

00:05:21.805 --> 00:05:23.741
than maybe when somebody else sings it

00:05:23.741 --> 00:05:27.000
'cause of nostalgia, because
I'm a fan, like whatever.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.340
But I think that's what's
so magical about music.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.740
It has new life, like with other artists.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.780
- Amen, and then let's talk
about the songwriter again.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.130
That's Dylan, right?

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.747
And what Dylan is so great about it,

00:05:36.747 --> 00:05:40.092
and what I'll try and do is
I'll try to impress you, right?

00:05:40.092 --> 00:05:42.270
I'll try and go, oh, that's clever.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.420
But Dylan just writes from there to here.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.557
- It's very straightforward, yeah.

00:05:46.557 --> 00:05:47.390
- Oh my God.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:51.090
And it's so simple, it's not simple,

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.220
if that makes any sense, it's brilliant.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.410
- Well, you have to be super
confident and comfortable

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.000
to keep it that like straight.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.262
- Amen.
- And yeah, I agree.

00:05:58.262 --> 00:05:59.512
- We're going again?

00:05:59.512 --> 00:06:00.345
- Yes!

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:02.294
You're welcome.

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:03.608
(Garth laughs)

00:06:03.608 --> 00:06:05.280
Oh boy, another one of your
daughters is embarrassed.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.697
- Aerosmith!
- Aerosmith.

00:06:06.697 --> 00:06:07.530
Now.
- Oh my gosh.

00:06:11.382 --> 00:06:13.895
- I am a hu, I thought I was
gonna marry Steven Tyler.

00:06:13.895 --> 00:06:14.790
(audience laughs)

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.083
I was like, ya ka ka ka ka kow!

00:06:16.083 --> 00:06:17.240
Like all it took, everywhere.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.650
I was like, I had a fan in my bedroom.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.383
I was like, yes, I was, yeah

00:06:21.383 --> 00:06:23.431
You gotta have a Aerosmith song.

00:06:23.431 --> 00:06:25.410
- Oh, I showered with him.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.640
- Oh wait, you covered the Fever.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.427
- Yeah, we covered Fever.
- Yeah!

00:06:28.427 --> 00:06:30.180
- But we were playing the last--

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.470
- Did you say, "I showered."
(audience laughs)

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.732
- I showered with him.

00:06:32.732 --> 00:06:35.723
So we're playing the last
play at Shea, Billy Joel.

00:06:35.723 --> 00:06:37.440
They're getting ready to
tear down Shea Stadium

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.584
in New York, and I go out
there and I'm late anyway,

00:06:40.584 --> 00:06:42.763
and they have just the baseball showers,

00:06:42.763 --> 00:06:45.029
and I'm in there showering and
getting ready for the show.

00:06:45.029 --> 00:06:47.160
And I had soap in my
eyes, and look around,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.697
and there's Steven Tyler,
he's showering too.

00:06:48.697 --> 00:06:50.640
"Hey, how you doin'?"
(audience laughs)

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.400
And so it's just, it was, how
many people get to say that?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.594
- Ah, no.

00:06:54.594 --> 00:06:59.252
Well, who knows?
(audience laughs)

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.085
Who knows?

00:07:00.085 --> 00:07:01.560
He's rock and roll, I don't know.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.393
- Beautiful can at the end of the day.

00:07:02.393 --> 00:07:03.964
- You might not be so special, Garth.

00:07:03.964 --> 00:07:05.970
(audience laughs)

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:06.960
- But I just love him.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.060
We were playing a writer's
night the other night

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.880
with Victoria Shaw and she
had a couple people get sick

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.800
and drop out and said, "Hey,
can you last minute pop on?"

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.633
I said, sure.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:16.203
She was playing with a
guy named Mark Hudson.

00:07:16.203 --> 00:07:20.111
So Mark wrote, Living On The Edge.

00:07:20.111 --> 00:07:20.944
♪ Living on the edge ♪

00:07:20.944 --> 00:07:22.890
- Oh my God, people, if you, right there,

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.056
when I said Living On The
Edge and you didn't go, "Ooh,"

00:07:25.056 --> 00:07:29.010
that's because Living
On The Edge has the line

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.104
of all lines when you
talk about songwriters.

00:07:31.104 --> 00:07:36.104
If you can judge a wise man
by the color of his skin,

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.660
then mister, you're a better man than I.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.772
- Yeah, it's great writing.
- Oh, oh my God.

00:07:41.772 --> 00:07:45.615
We wait our whole life to try
to write a line like that.

00:07:45.615 --> 00:07:46.603
Right.
- Yeah.

00:07:46.603 --> 00:07:47.966
- I just, I love his stuff.

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:49.770
But Aerosmith, yeah, we did Fever.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.300
There's no way I could do Fever on here.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.520
It's just a bunch of rah kind of stuff.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.353
But it's--

00:07:54.353 --> 00:07:55.186
- Which is incredible.

00:07:55.186 --> 00:07:56.220
- He's unbelievable.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:57.373
But anything he does--

00:07:57.373 --> 00:07:59.940
- Anything you do though
right now is still not gonna,

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.200
we're all still thinking about you

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.190
and Steve and Tyler in the shower.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.870
- Yeah, well, yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:04.703
- Okay, next one.

00:08:04.703 --> 00:08:06.210
I love Aerosmith and I'm still thinking

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.080
of y'all in the shower.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.374
Here we go, next one.

00:08:08.374 --> 00:08:10.413
- That was three for three.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:12.413
- [Kelly] I know, but
look, you're good at it.

00:08:12.413 --> 00:08:13.246
- [Garth] What do we got?

00:08:13.246 --> 00:08:14.940
Kiss.
- Ooh.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.120
- I know you like Kiss.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.020
- Kiss, so they had a tribute
album called Kiss My Ass.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:19.853
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:08:19.853 --> 00:08:20.686
- Remember this tribute album?

00:08:20.686 --> 00:08:21.519
- Yes.

00:08:21.519 --> 00:08:22.352
And they said, "Do you wanna sing on it?"

00:08:22.352 --> 00:08:23.850
And I said, well,

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.656
I'm thinking I'm the
only country guy on it.

00:08:25.656 --> 00:08:29.370
'Cause in 1980 we had
an old boom in Oklahoma.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.350
We talked about this in the Vegas show.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:34.440
And all these guys moved in
from states that I never knew.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.014
And some guys came down from Michigan

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:37.853
and they had the Kiss albums.

00:08:37.853 --> 00:08:39.705
And we became best buddies.

00:08:39.705 --> 00:08:42.267
And so I was like, yeah, I wanna sing.

00:08:42.267 --> 00:08:45.789
I wanna sing either Detroit Rock City,

00:08:45.789 --> 00:08:48.989
or you know,

00:08:48.989 --> 00:08:51.300
♪ I wanna a rock and roll ♪

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.556
And they're like, "No, no."

00:08:52.556 --> 00:08:53.640
- What?

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.990
- I was like, "No, really?"

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.730
I said just, I didn't wanna do Beth.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.830
I mean, I'm sorry, but
if you're a Kiss fan,

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.444
Beth was the one ballad that they.

00:09:00.444 --> 00:09:01.277
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:01.277 --> 00:09:02.891
- And they let me do, what was it?

00:09:02.891 --> 00:09:07.452
♪ If ever I'd met you ♪

00:09:07.452 --> 00:09:11.265
♪ I'd never have seen you cry ♪

00:09:11.265 --> 00:09:14.162
♪ If not for the first hello ♪

00:09:14.162 --> 00:09:17.670
♪ We'd never have to say goodbye ♪

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.265
- Right, I got to do

00:09:19.265 --> 00:09:20.865
♪ Rags ♪

00:09:20.865 --> 00:09:23.370
♪ A sailors only daughter. ♪

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.571
And it was cool because the two Erics

00:09:25.571 --> 00:09:28.110
were with them then,
Peter, Chris, and Ace Free,

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.999
they weren't with them when
they were doing this record,

00:09:29.999 --> 00:09:32.748
but it was Paul and Gene
and then the two Erics.

00:09:32.748 --> 00:09:35.213
And you're standing there in the studio

00:09:35.213 --> 00:09:37.069
where you cut Friends In Low Places,

00:09:37.069 --> 00:09:38.760
and there's Gene Simmons

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.120
who can't play on a record sitting down.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.520
So he has to stand up and
he's, without the heels,

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.061
he's 6'6 anyway, right?
- Really?

00:09:46.061 --> 00:09:46.894
Yeah.

00:09:46.894 --> 00:09:47.850
- And he's got it way down by his knees,

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:48.683
and he's playing it.

00:09:48.683 --> 00:09:50.700
I'm going, this is the
fricking coolest thing.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.836
And they both look great.

00:09:51.836 --> 00:09:55.388
But they're both, Paul
Stanley's gotta be 6'4.

00:09:55.388 --> 00:09:58.707
You know, Gene has to be 6'5, 6'6.

00:09:58.707 --> 00:09:59.760
- And they wear heels!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.797
- And then they get in the heels.

00:10:00.797 --> 00:10:01.800
- Yeah.
- That's crazy.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.030
- Because I've been in a picture with them

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.826
and I looked like an Oompa Loompa.

00:10:04.826 --> 00:10:06.255
- We all do. (laughs)

00:10:06.255 --> 00:10:07.993
- Yeah, I was like, not today.

00:10:07.993 --> 00:10:08.880
- We all do, they were sweet.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.590
No, I was like, Hey Kiss is coming here,

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.810
let's screw everything down
so they can't steal anything.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:13.680
Right.
(Kelly laughs)

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.092
And they came in and
they were the nicest guys

00:10:16.092 --> 00:10:17.246
on the planet.

00:10:17.246 --> 00:10:20.040
They had baby pictures, all this stuff.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.920
And I tell you anything they
ever wanna do, count me in.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:23.940
'Cause I love those guys.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.670
- Yeah, I run into them
once with Reba actually.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.260
And they were so nice, they were so cool.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.490
But I was like, really?

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:30.366
You were already tall enough.

00:10:30.366 --> 00:10:32.130
You didn't have to wear
those, like I was like.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.920
- So I don't know if
showering with Steven Tyler

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.342
might be weirder than I ran
into them with Reba McIntyre.

00:10:37.342 --> 00:10:39.300
- No, no, showering with Steven Tyler

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.220
definitely tops it all.
- Really?

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.455
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:10:41.455 --> 00:10:43.320
That tops it all.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.140
No, we were at the ACMs,
we were doing the ACMs

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.970
and they were there, and
then all of a sudden,

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.590
I came out and she was like,
"Kelly, get in the picture."

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:51.030
And I was like, what?

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.620
And then, and I was just in a picture

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.050
with Kiss and Reba, and I
was like, I love my life,

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:55.936
I was like--

00:10:55.936 --> 00:10:57.030
- How cool is that though?

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:59.430
Somebody was thinking,
because I saw those guys

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.003
in '81, '80 maybe.

00:11:03.003 --> 00:11:07.136
And then I saw 'em in 2010,
2009, something like that.

00:11:07.136 --> 00:11:08.717
In the makeup.

00:11:08.717 --> 00:11:10.144
- They look the same.

00:11:10.144 --> 00:11:11.744
- Pfft, they do, they look exactly--

00:11:11.744 --> 00:11:13.137
- You never age, yes.

00:11:13.137 --> 00:11:14.340
- No, it's so smart.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.173
- I know.

00:11:15.173 --> 00:11:17.063
Okay, that was Rockstar
Roulette, everybody.

00:11:17.063 --> 00:11:21.024
Give it up for Garth Brooks!
(audience cheers)

00:11:21.024 --> 00:11:23.328
- His Las Vegas residency,
Garth Brooks Plus One

00:11:23.328 --> 00:11:25.918
begins tonight at Caesar's
Palace Colosseum in Las Vegas.

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:28.170
You've gotta go see it,
it's an amazing show.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.173
You're gonna love it,
go online for tickets.

